ntEnums[i]);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                return result;\n            };\n        }());\n    }\n\n})();\n\n/**\n *\n * Define Logger component\n *\n * @constructor\n * @param {object} options\n * @returns {object} Logger\n *\n * Declaration example.\n * var logger = new Logger({\n *    d: { prefix: \"[DEBUG] => \", color: \"blue\" },\n *    i: { prefix: \"[INFO] => \", color: \"green\" },\n *    e: { prefix: \"[ERROR] => \", color: \"red\" }\n * });\n *\n * We have dynamically created d(), i(), e() methods for logging messages with the defined prefixes and colors.\n *\n */\n\n\"use strict\";\n\nfunction Logger(options) {\n\n    ubi._classCallCheck(this, Logger);\n\n    //typeof options !== 'object' ? function() { throw new TypeError(\"No object\"); } : null;\n    if (typeof options === 'undefined') {\n        console.log(\"%cLogger defined with the default values.\\nUse '.log()' method to print messages or '.o()' to print objects.\", 'color: orange');\n    }\n\n    // A default method to print messages\n    var log = function (message, stackTrace) {\n        stackTrace ? console.trace() : null;\n        this.print(message);\n    };\n\n    var print = function (message, stackTrace, prefix, color) {\n        stackTrace = typeof stackTrace === 'undefined' ? false : stackTrace;\n        prefix = typeof prefix === 'undefined' ? \"\" : prefix;\n        color = typeof color === 'undefined' ? \"black\" : color;\n\n        stackTrace ? console.trace() : null;\n        ubi.isDevMode() ? console.log('%c' + prefix + message, 'color:' + color) : null;\n    };\n\n    // Dynamically create methods according to the options object\n    var tempThis = this;\n    Object.keys(options).forEach(function (v) {\n        tempThis[v] = function (message, stackTrace) {\n            print(message, stackTrace, options[v].prefix, options[v].color);\n        };\n    });\n};\n\n// Attach a method for printing objects\nLogger.prototype.o = function (message, stackTrace) {\n    //typeof message !== 'object' ? logger.e(\"No javascript object found. Use this method to print javascript objects.\") : null;\n\n    stackTrace ? console.trace() : null;\n    ubi.isDevMode() ? console.log(message) : null;\n};\n\n// .die() is method to log something and stop code execution\nLogger.prototype.die = function (message, stackTrace) {\n    stackTrace ? console.trace() : null;\n    ubi.isDevMode() ? console.log(message) : null;\n    throw new Error(\"EXECUTION STOPPED!!\");\n};\n\n/**\n * Define Routing component as an extension of page.js (https://visionmedia.github.io/page.js) plugin\n *\n * @constructor\n * @param {function} preExecute - Execute code before start POST request\n * @param {function} postExecute - Execute code after POST request is completed\n * @returns {object} Road - The routing object\n */\n\nfunction Road(preExecute, postExecute, postExecuteAnonymous) {\n\n    \"use strict\";\n\n    ubi._classCallCheck(this, Road);\n\n    var _self = this;\n\n    this.preExecute = preExecute;\n    this.postExecute = postExecute;\n    this.postExecuteAnonymous = postExecuteAnonymous;\n\n    // Add methods\n    this.load = function(ctx, next) {\n        if (typeof _self.preExecute !== 'undefined' && typeof _self.preExecute === 'function') {\n            _self.preExecute(ctx, next);\n        } else {\n            // Basic code for load method\n            ubi.loader.nonBlocking.start();\n            $.post(ctx.canonicalPath, function (data) {\n                logger.i(\"Current page set to: \" + ctx.canonicalPath);\n                ctx.htmlData = data;\n                next();\n            });\n        }\n    };\n\n    this.show = function(exec) {\n        return function(ctx) {\n            if (typeof _self.postExecute !== 'undefined' && typeof _self.postExecute === 'function') {\n                _self.postExecute(ctx);\n            } else {\n                // Basic code for show method\n\n                // Paste HTML (fragment)\n                $(\"#content\").html(ctx.htmlData);\n                // Try to activate the page's menu item\n                $('#menu-' + ctx.pathname.split(\"/\")[1]).addClass('active');\n                // Set browser's title\n                var pageTitle = $(\"#main h1\").text()\n                document.title = pageTitle != \"\" ? ubi.APP_NAME + \" | \" + pageTitle : ubi.APP_NAME;\n                // Stop blocking loader\n                ubi.loader.nonBlocking.stop();\n            }\n\n            // Callback execution\n            if (typeof exec === 'function') {\n                exec(ctx);\n            } else if (typeof exec !== 'undefined') {\n                throw new TypeError(exec + ' is not a function')\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    this.showAnonymous = function (exec) {\n        return function (ctx) {\n            if (typeof _self.postExecuteAnonymous !== 'undefined' && typeof _self.postExecuteAnonymous === 'function') {\n                _self.postExecuteAnonymous(ctx);\n            } else {\n                // Basic code for show method\n\n                // Paste HTML (fragment)\n                $(\"#layout-container\").html(ctx.htmlData);\n                // Set browser's title\n                var pageTitle = $(\"#layout-container h1\").text();\n                document.title = pageTitle != \"\" ? ubi.APP_NAME + \" | \" + pageTitle : ubi.APP_NAME;\n                // Stop blocking loader\n                ubi.loader.nonBlocking.stop();\n            }\n\n            // Callback execution\n            if (typeof exec === 'function') {\n                exec(ctx);\n            } else if (typeof exec !== 'undefined') {\n                throw new TypeError(exec + ' is not a function')\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    this.addRoutePost = function(routePath, exec) {\n        page(routePath, this.load, this.show(exec));\n    };\n\n    this.addRouteCallback = function(routePath, callback) {\n        page(routePath, callback);\n    };\n\n    this.addRouteAnonymousPost = function(routePath, exec) {\n        page(routePath, this.load, this.showAnonymous(exec));\n    };\n\n    this.base = function(routePath) { page.base(routePath) };\n\n    this.init = function() { page() };\n\n};\n\n/**\n * SockJS-client/Stomp wrapper\n */\n\nfunction socketWrap() {\n\n    'use strict';\n\n    var client = {}; // stomp object\n    var topicsMem = [];\n\n    var s = {\n        topics: [], // topics Array\n        reconnect: true, // if you'd like to reconnect when socket lose its connection\n        dev: false, // environment mode\n\n        /*\n         * Set debug for stomp protocol debugging messages\n         *\n         * @param {boolean} hasDebug - The topics you would like to subscribe\n         */\n        setDebug: function(debug) {\n            if (debug && s.dev) {\n                client.debug = function(str) {\n                    console.log(str);\n                }\n            }\n            else {\n                client.debug = null;\n            }\n        },\n\n        isConnected: function() {\n            if ('connected' in client) return client.connected;\n        },\n\n        /*\n         * Use this method to connect.\n         *\n         * @param {Array} topics - The topics you would like to subscribe\n         * @param {function} reconCallback - Execute a function after a reconnection is requested\n         */\n        connect: function(endpoint, onConnectCallback, reconCallback) {\n            if (endpoint === undefined) { //|| !Array.isArray(s.topics) || s.topics.length === 0) {\n                throw new TypeError(\"You need to set an endpoint uri and at least one topic like [{ url: 'topic_url', call: function }]. Use setTopics() method.\");\n            }\n            // init socket\n            var sockjs = new SockJS(endpoint);\n            client = Stomp.over(sockjs);\n            // debugging by default is disabled\n            s.setDebug(false);\n\n            client.connect({}, function (frame) {\n                client.debug != null ? console.log('Connected: ' + frame) : null;\n                s.dev ? console.log('WebSocket connection established') : null;\n\n                typeof onConnectCallback === 'function' ? onConnectCallback() : null;\n\n            }, function() {\n                if (!s.reconnect) {\n                    console.log(\"WebSocket closed\");\n                    return;\n                }//else\n                // TODO - reconnection counter property\n                s.dev ? console.warn(\"WebSocket closed. Try to reconnect\") : null;\n                setTimeout(function() {\n                    s.connect(endpoint, onConnectCallback);\n                }, 2000);\n            });\n        },\n\n        disconnect: function() {\n            client.disconnect(function() {\n                s.dev ? console.log(\"Successfully disconnected from WebSocket\") : null;\n            });\n        },\n\n        subscribe: function(topic) {\n            if (typeof topic === 'undefined' || (typeof topic !== 'object' && !(('url' in topic) || ('call' in topic)))) {\n                throw new TypeError(\"You have to pass a topic argument that must be an object like { url: 'topic_url', call: function }\");\n            }\n\n            if (s.isSubscribed(topic.id)) {\n                console.warn(\"Already subscribed to topic: \" + topic.id);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            var tid = client.subscribe(topic.url, topic.call).id;\n            topic.tid = tid;\n            s.topics.push(topic);\n\n            return tid;\n        },\n\n        unsubscribe: function(id) {\n            // TODO - need optimization\n            var topic = s.topics.filter(function(obj) {\n                return obj.id === id;\n            });\n\n            var index = s.topics.map(function (obj) {\n                return obj.id;\n            }).indexOf(id);\n            s.topics.splice(index, 1);\n\n            if (topic.length === 1) {\n                // pop out from topics array\n                client.unsubscribe(topic[0].tid);\n            } else {\n                s.dev ? console.warn(\"Couldn't find topic with id: \" + id) : null;\n                return false;\n            }\n        },\n\n        isSubscribed: function (id) {\n            var topic = s.topics.filter(function(obj) {\n                return obj.id === id;\n            });\n            return topic.length === 1 ? true : false;\n        },\n\n        unsubscribeAll: function() {\n            var i;\n\n            for (i in s.topics) {\n                client.unsubscribe(s.topics[i].tid);\n            }\n        }\n\n    };\n\n    return s;\n\n}\n/**\n * ubiSetup contains a global object that stores properties and methods which used in order to properly run your application.\n */\n\n(function ($this) {\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  // Create the entities ubi object\n  $this.ubi = new Object();\n\n  ubi._classCallCheck = function (instance, Constructor) {\n    if (!(instance instanceof Constructor)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"Cannot call a class as a function\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Return true if current mode is set to development\n   *\n   * @returns {Boolean}\n   */\n  var isDevMode = function () {\n    //TODO - Get this value from application.properties\n    return this.ENV_MODE === \"DEV\";\n  };\n\n  // Define static immutable properties and methods\n  Object.defineProperties(ubi, {\n    // Properties\n    LOGGED_IN: {value: \"islg\"},\n    // Methods\n    isDevMode: {value: isDevMode}\n  });\n\n  // Define redirect page\n  ubi.redirectTopage = $(\"#redirect-to-page\").val();  \n    \n  ubi.setLogin = function (login) {\n    localStorage[this.LOGGED_IN] = login;\n  };\n  ubi.hasAccess = function () {\n    // todo need something more sophisticated\n    return localStorage.getItem(this.LOGGED_IN) !== null;\n  };\n  ubi.removeAccess = function () {\n    localStorage.removeItem(this.LOGGED_IN);\n  };\n\n  ubi.goHome = function (lang) { \n    if (lang != null) {\n      page.redirect(\"/?lang=\"+lang);  \n    } else {\n      page.redirect(\"/\");\n    }\n  };\n\n  ubi.setTitle = function (title) {\n    var pageTitle = typeof title !== 'undefined' ? title : $(\"h1\").text();\n    document.title = pageTitle != \"\" ? ubi.APP_NAME + \" | \" + pageTitle\n        : ubi.APP_NAME;\n  };\n\n  //Setup JQuery Pre-filter\n  ubi.setupAjaxCallFiltering = function () {\n    $.ajaxPrefilter(function (options, originalOptions, jqXHR) {\n      options.async = true;\n    });\n    logger.d(\"AJAX call filtering has been setup\");\n  };\n\n  // Locale\n  ubi.setLocale = function () {\n    $.post(\"/header?lang=\" + document.getElementById('lang').value,\n        function (data) {\n          $(\"#header\").html(data);\n        });\n\n    $.post(\"/content?lang=\" + document.getElementById('lang').value,\n        function (data) {\n          $(\"#content\").html(data);\n        });\n  };\n\n  // Detect touch devices\n  ubi.isTouchDevice = function () {\n    return (bowser.mobile !== undefined && bowser.mobile) || (bowser.tablet\n        !== undefined && bowser.tablet);\n  };\n\n  /*\n   * Animate scroll to a specific element\n   *\n   * @param element - The dom element path\n   * @param offset - If you need extra offset for scroll movement\n   * @param animateSpeed - Set the animation speed. Set 0 if you don't want animation\n   * @param calcElementHeight - Boolean value. Set to true only if you need to calculate also the extra height of the element that you want to scrool to\n   */\n  ubi.scrollToSpecificElement = function (element, offset, animateSpeed,\n      calcElementHeight) {\n    var elementTop = $(element).offset().top;\n    if (calcElementHeight) {\n      elementTop = elementTop - $(element).outerHeight() - offset;\n    }\n\n    $(\"html, body\").animate({scrollTop: elementTop}, animateSpeed);\n  };\n\n  ubi.filtersSearch = function filtersSearch(id) {\n    if (event.keyCode == 13) {\n      tb.filter($('#' + id));\n    }\n  }\n\n  ubi.addCityToCountry = function ($this) {\n\n    if (!ubi.addCityToCountry.store) {\n\n      let existingCitiesObj = $(\n          \"#existingCitiesObj\").val();\n\n      if (existingCitiesObj !== undefined\n          && existingCitiesObj !== '') {\n\n        let jsonCC = JSON.parse(existingCitiesObj);\n        if (jsonCC.length > 0) {\n\n          ubi.addCityToCountry.store = [];\n\n          for (let i = 0; i < jsonCC.length; i++) {\n\n            ubi.addCityToCountry.store.push({\n              \"id\": jsonCC[i].id,\n              \"name\": jsonCC[i].name\n            });\n\n          }\n\n        } else {\n          ubi.addCityToCountry.store = [];\n        }\n\n      } else {\n        ubi.addCityToCountry.store = [];\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    if (!ubi.addCityToCountry.counter) {\n\n      let existingCitiesObj = $(\n          \"#existingCitiesObj\").val();\n\n      if (existingCitiesObj !== undefined\n          && existingCitiesObj !== '') {\n\n        let jsonCC = JSON.parse(existingCitiesObj);\n\n        if (jsonCC.length > 0) {\n\n          ubi.addCityToCountry.counter = jsonCC.length;\n\n        } else {\n          ubi.addCityToCountry.counter = 0;\n        }\n\n      } else {\n        ubi.addCityToCountry.counter = 0;\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    // let field = $('#cities-wrapper').serializeJSON(serializeJSON_OPTIONS);\n\n    if ($('#cityName').val() === undefined || $('#cityName').val() === '') {\n      alertify.error(\"Fill all the fields and then click the \\\"add\\\" button\");\n      return;\n    }\n\n    let $fieldset = $('fieldset#cities-wrapper');\n    $fieldset.children('.body').addClass('hidden');\n    $fieldset.children('.table-wrapper').removeClass('hidden');\n\n    ubi.addCityToCountry.store.push({\n      \"name\": $('#cityName').val()\n    });\n\n    let counter = (++ubi.addCityToCountry.counter);\n\n    $fieldset.children('.table-wrapper').find('tbody').append(\n        '<tr>' +\n        '<td><input t